---
/**
 * CONTACT — correspondence.
 * ============================================================================
 * The last sheet in the archive, and the only one addressed to someone.
 *
 * Seven worlds document: what was built, how the intelligence in it works,
 * where the source is, what is being learned. This one stops documenting. That
 * change of mode is the design problem — the page has to read as the natural
 * final action of an archive rather than as the thing bolted to the end of a
 * portfolio, which is why it is a letter and not a card with three icons on it.
 *
 * ── Three decisions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * 1. NO FORM, AND THE PAGE SAYS WHY. This site is static HTML on GitHub Pages.
 *    There is no server, so a form would need a third party to receive it —
 *    and the version that gets built by accident is worse: one that validates,
 *    clears itself, prints "message sent" and transmits nothing. Clause 04 is
 *    that reasoning, published, because an unexplained absence reads as an
 *    oversight and an explained one reads as a decision.
 *
 * 2. THREE CHANNELS, NOT SIX. V1 publishes six. Three are carried forward;
 *    two personal social accounts and a WhatsApp link containing a mobile
 *    number are not. They passed verification — they failed relevance, and in
 *    the phone number's case a privacy judgement that belongs to its owner
 *    rather than to a page being rebuilt. See the note in `lib/contact.ts`.
 *
 * 3. SUBJECTS, NOT AVAILABILITY. Clause 01 lists what a correspondence can be
 *    ABOUT. It does not say "open for work", because this archive holds no
 *    employment status, no capacity and no notice period, and clause 05 names
 *    those absences rather than leaving them to be assumed.
 *
 * ── Client JavaScript ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * None. The mail link is a plain `mailto:`, and the address is also the link
 * text, so it can be copied by anyone with no mail client registered. Nothing
 * on this page needs a script to be usable, which is the correct property for
 * the one page a visitor arrives at in order to do something.
 */
import WorldLayout from '@layouts/WorldLayout.astro';
import TitleBlock, { type Cell } from '@components/projects/TitleBlock.astro';
import { getWorld } from '@lib/worlds';
import { PROFILE } from '@lib/profile';
import { CHANNELS, MATTERS, UNLISTED } from '@lib/contact';
import '@styles/contact.css';

const world = getWorld('contact');

const cells: Cell[] = [
  { key: 'Sheet', value: `${world.ref} · Contact`, accent: true },
  { key: 'Channels', value: `${CHANNELS.length}, all verified` },
  { key: 'Form', value: 'None — see 04' },
  { key: 'Reply', value: 'No time promised' },
];

/** External links need the mark and the rel; `mailto:` needs neither. */
const isExternal = (href: string) => href.startsWith('http');
---

<WorldLayout
  world="contact"
  title="Contact"
  description="Three verified ways to write to Ayush Rijal — email, GitHub and LinkedIn. No form, because this site is static and a form with nowhere to send would be a lie."
  masthead={false}
>
  <div class="sheet letter">
    <p class="t-label letter__mark">
      <span>{world.ref} · {world.gateTitle}</span>
      <span>{world.world}</span>
    </p>
    <hr class="rule rule--strong" />

    <h1 class="t-display letter__title">Correspondence</h1>
    <p class="t-text letter__lede">
      Everything before this sheet is a record. This one is a channel: the point
      where the archive stops describing what has been done and a person answers.
    </p>

    <TitleBlock cells={cells} label="Correspondence details" />

    {/* The reference block — the archive's only end-aligned furniture. */}
    <dl class="refs" aria-label="Sheet references">
      <div class="refs__row">
        <dt class="t-label refs__key">Compiled</dt>
        <dd class="refs__value">{world.ref} · Ayush Rijal Archive</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="refs__row">
        <dt class="t-label refs__key">Preceding sheets</dt>
        <dd class="refs__value">AR-00 to AR-06</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="refs__row">
        <dt class="t-label refs__key">This sheet</dt>
        <dd class="refs__value refs__value--accent">Open</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <div class="body">
      {/* ── 01 The standing invitation ──────────────────────────────── */}
      <section class="clause" aria-labelledby="invitation">
        <h2 class="t-label clause__head" id="invitation">
          <span class="clause__no">01</span>
          <span class="clause__title">What this channel is for</span>
        </h2>

        <p class="invitation">
          If you have something worth building, investigating, challenging or
          discussing, open a correspondence.
        </p>

        <p class="t-text clause__lede">
          Five subjects, in no order of preference. This is a list of what a
          letter here can be <em>about</em> — not a list of services, and not a
          statement of availability, which is a claim this archive does not
          hold and clause 05 says so.
        </p>

        <ol class="matters" role="list">
          {
            MATTERS.map((m, i) => (
              <li class="matter">
                <span class="t-label matter__no">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
                <span class="matter__name">{m.name}</span>
                <p class="matter__gloss">{m.gloss}</p>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
      </section>

      {/* ── 02 The correspondent ────────────────────────────────────── */}
      <section class="clause" aria-labelledby="correspondent">
        <h2 class="t-label clause__head" id="correspondent">
          <span class="clause__no">02</span>
          <span class="clause__title">Correspondent</span>
        </h2>

        <div class="correspondent">
          <p class="correspondent__name">{PROFILE.name}</p>
          <ul class="correspondent__roles" role="list">
            {PROFILE.identity.primary.map((role) => <li>{role}</li>)}
            <li class="correspondent__roles-secondary">
              {PROFILE.identity.secondary}
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p class="t-text correspondent__where">
          {PROFILE.education.level} at {PROFILE.education.institution}, currently
          working through {PROFILE.learning.join(', ')}. The rest of the record
          is on the <a href="/about">personal sheet</a>, and what is being
          learned — with the evidence for each line — is in the{' '}
          <a href="/learning">field notebook</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      {/* ── 03 Channels ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
      <section class="clause" aria-labelledby="channels">
        <h2 class="t-label clause__head" id="channels">
          <span class="clause__no">03</span>
          <span class="clause__title">Open channels</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="t-text clause__lede">
          Three, and each one states where its value was read from. A contact
          address is the one fact on a site that fails silently when it is
          wrong — nobody writes back to tell you.
        </p>

        <ul class="channels" role="list">
          {
            CHANNELS.map((c) => (
              <li class="channel">
                <span class="t-label channel__label">
                  {c.label}
                  {c.primary && <span class="channel__primary"> · preferred</span>}
                </span>
                <a
                  class="channel__value"
                  href={c.href}
                  rel={isExternal(c.href) ? 'noopener noreferrer' : undefined}
                >
                  {c.value}
                  {isExternal(c.href) && (
                    <span class="ext" aria-hidden="true">
                      {' '}
                      &#8599;
                    </span>
                  )}
                </a>
                <span class="t-label channel__basis">{c.verifiedBy}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </section>

      {/* ── 04 There is no form ─────────────────────────────────────── */}
      <section class="clause" aria-labelledby="noform">
        <h2 class="t-label clause__head" id="noform">
          <span class="clause__no">04</span>
          <span class="clause__title">There is no form on this page</span>
        </h2>

        <div class="t-text noform">
          <p>
            This site is a directory of static HTML files served by GitHub
            Pages. There is no server behind it, which is deliberate — it is
            also why no credential exists anywhere in this archive to be
            leaked. It does mean there is nowhere for a submitted message to
            arrive.
          </p>
          <p>
            A form here would have to hand your message and your address to a
            third-party service: a company neither of us chose, under a privacy
            policy neither of us read, for the sake of a text box. That is a
            real cost paid by you, to save one click by me.
          </p>
          <p>
            The alternative is worse and it is the one that gets built by
            accident — a form that validates, clears itself and prints{' '}
            <strong>message sent</strong> while transmitting nothing. It works
            perfectly in every test and lies to the one visitor who most wanted
            to reach you.
          </p>
          <p>
            So the address in clause 03 is the mechanism. It is a
            <code> mailto:</code> link and also plain text, so it works whether
            or not you have a mail client, with or without JavaScript. It goes
            to a person.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      {/* ── 05 Not on this sheet ────────────────────────────────────── */}
      <section class="clause" aria-labelledby="unlisted">
        <h2 class="t-label clause__head" id="unlisted">
          <span class="clause__no">05</span>
          <span class="clause__title">Not on this sheet</span>
        </h2>

        <ul class="unlisted" role="list">
          {UNLISTED.map((field) => <li>{field}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <p class="unlisted__note">
          None of these is recorded anywhere in the archive, so none of them
          appears here. They are named individually rather than quietly omitted,
          because a contact page that simply leaves out rates reads as
          expensive, and one that leaves out availability reads as unavailable.
          Neither is a thing this page knows.
        </p>
        <p class="unlisted__note">
          Social accounts are not indexed here either. They exist; this is a
          correspondence sheet rather than a directory, and the address above
          reaches the same person faster.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="t-text signoff">
        The archive is still being written. If you find something in it that is
        wrong, that is the most useful letter you can send.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</WorldLayout>
